## Errors & Mistakes
The initial protocol test covered only the successful response and did not exercise the error branches implemented in the client or their conversion into Terraform diagnostics. The first focused Go test in an earlier revision could not read the build cache under the restricted process sandbox and reported an operation-not-permitted error; it passed with normal process permissions. An earlier GitHub CLI request for a failed acceptance job log could not connect to api.github.com; the retry succeeded. The original public interface called principal.uid user_id, which was too narrow for service-account identities. Acceptance CI for unrelated suites failed on object-storage convergence and unavailable inference capacity; the caller identity suite passed. The one permitted inference rerun failed again because the configured QA capacity was unavailable, so it was not rerun again.

## Dead Ends
No existing provider dependency exposes this identity route. Adding a schema dependency was unnecessary for a two-field read, so the implementation uses the authenticated JSON endpoint and the provider's existing HTTP client. Leaving the live test in the root package would have made it manual-only, so the data source uses a suite-shaped package even though it has no resources to sweep. A user_id compatibility alias was not added because the attribute has not shipped and the alias would preserve a misleading name. The error tests remain protocol-level rather than duplicating client-only tests because this route covers both coreweave/caller_identity.go and the Terraform diagnostic boundary. The acceptance-test selection logic was not broadened because the repository's normal unit test job already runs this package for Go changes. Unrelated acceptance failures were diagnosed but not changed in this pull request.

## Hints for Future Agents
The JSON response maps principal.orgUid to organization_id and principal.uid to principal_id. Connect interceptors do not apply to the direct JSON request, so the request must attach the configured bearer token and user agent. Keep the schema at two computed attributes unless the public product contract expands. Preserve the protocol-level error table when changing response decoding or diagnostics. Update both the make suite list and workflow suite list when renaming or removing the acceptance package. Preserve the cross-cloud comparison in public metadata and generated documentation, but do not claim identical semantics.

## Codebase Discoveries
Data sources are registered by the provider's DataSources method. Documentation is generated from examples and provider schemas with make generate. A schema MarkdownDescription is rendered into both the data-source page body and its frontmatter description. The shared retryable HTTP client supplies the existing timeout and retry behavior to the identity request. Acceptance suites are selected independently by GNUmakefile and the pull request workflow; root-package acceptance tests are not included. Tests in the calleridentity package can exercise the root CoreWeave client through the configured Terraform protocol server, including errors returned as Terraform diagnostics. Object-storage policy schemas use principal terminology for identities that can include users, roles, and groups. The AWS caller identity data source calls STS GetCallerIdentity. AzureRM client config reads client, tenant, subscription, and object IDs from provider state. Google client OpenID userinfo calls the OpenID userinfo endpoint and requires the userinfo.email scope.

